Each file argument with an unsupported extension (`.txt`), nested path included, gets its own error on stderr, so stdout is empty and outln exits 1.
== args
alpha.txt
nested/beta.txt
== file alpha.txt
const alpha = 1;
== file nested/beta.txt
const beta = 2;
== stdout
== stderr
File alpha.txt has an unsupported file type; supported: .md, .ts, .mts, .cts, .tsx, .js, .jsx, .mjs, .cjs, .rs, .css, .json, .jsonc, .toml, .yaml, .yml
File nested/beta.txt has an unsupported file type; supported: .md, .ts, .mts, .cts, .tsx, .js, .jsx, .mjs, .cjs, .rs, .css, .json, .jsonc, .toml, .yaml, .yml
== exit 1
